367 - Rescue the Perishing
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 367
Topic: Christian Church - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]Rescue the perishing,
Care [Eb]for the dy[Bb]ing;
[F]Snatch them in [Bb]pity from [F]sin [C7]and the [F]grave;
[Bb]Weep o’er the erring one,
Lift [F]up the fal[Bb]len,
[F]Tell them of [Bb]Jesus, the [Eb]might[F7]y to [Bb]save.
[F]Rescue the [Bb]perishing,
[F]Care for the [Bb]dying;
[Eb]Jesus is [Bb]merciful,
[Eb]Jesus [F7]will [Bb]save.

Refrain:
[Bb]Rescue the perishing, care for the dying;
[Eb]Jesus is merciful, [Bb]Jesus will save.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Though they are slighting him, still he is waiting,
[Eb]waiting the penitent [Bb]child to receive;
[F]plead [Bb]with them [F]earnestly, [C7]plead with [F]them gently;
[Bb]he will forgive if they only believe.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Rescue the perishing, duty demands it;
[Eb]strength for thy labor [Bb]the Lord will provide;
[F]back [Bb]to the [F]narrow [C7]way patiently [F]win them;
[Bb]tell the poor wanderer a Savior has died.
